@cc ===========================================================================
@cc TESTUI:MODE - build the PLANC-SCREEN-H / VTM screen demo on D100.
@cc
@cc   @MODE TESTUI:MODE,,
@cc
@cc Needs these under SYSTEM before it will link:
@cc
@cc   TESTUI:PLNC       the source
@cc   SCREEN:SYMB       the PLANC-SCREEN-H interface, $INCLUDEd by the source
@cc   INTRF1B:BRF       the PLANC-SCREEN-H 1-bank runtime (INTERF-1B renamed)
@cc   VTMR:BRF          VTM routines - off the FOCUS floppy ND-10188. WITHOUT THESE the
@cc   VTMDATA:BRF       link leaves nine VT* entries undefined and the program misbehaves.
@cc   VTMARR:BRF        VTMCPOS and VTMCPAR are NOT needed - VTMR already defines them.
@cc
@cc SCREEN:SYMB and INTRF1B:BRF come off the PLANC-SCREEN-H floppy and are
@cc NOT part of a stock SINTRAN - see README.md in the repo folder for where
@cc they come from and how to put them on. MON-CALL-1B-A00 and PLANC-1BANK-F00
@cc are already on D100.
@cc
@cc LIBRARY-MODE ON means a library hands over only the units something has
@cc already asked for, so loading MON-CALL-1B-A00 costs nothing if the screen
@cc library turns out not to call into it. The vendor demo's header says it is
@cc needed, so it is loaded rather than guessed about.
@cc
@cc READ WHAT LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED PRINTS. An undefined entry does NOT fail
@cc the build - BRF-LINKER still writes a runnable TESTUI:PROG that then
@cc misbehaves in ways that look like a bug in the program. Anything listed is
@cc a library missing or loaded in the wrong order.
@cc
@cc In particular: the vendor demo's header comment says Vtm must be loaded
@cc with the program. Whether that means a VTM BRF has to appear in this LOAD
@cc list, or whether the VTM routines are already inside SINTRAN and only the
@cc DDBTABLES:VTM data file matters, is NOT known. This is the command that
@cc answers it: if VTM symbols come out undefined, a VTM array BRF is needed.
@cc ===========================================================================
@DELETE-FILE TESTUI:PROG
@DELETE-FILE TESTUI:LIST
@DELETE-FILE TESTUI:BRF
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE TESTUI:PLNC,"TESTUI:LIST","TESTUI"
EXIT
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "TESTUI"
LOAD TESTUI
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD INTRF1B
LOAD VTMR
LOAD VTMDATA
LOAD VTMARR
LOAD MON-CALL-1B-A00
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT
